       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the maximum, so I want to confirm it with you first.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** This is about twice the maximum daily dose. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), which may be what you intended.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day).\n- **500 mg PO twice daily or 850 mg PO once daily**, if you're starting therapy. Metformin is usually started low and titrated up.\n\nIf you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and give me the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
